# llm-auto-router example environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` (which is gitignored; keep it chmod 600) and fill in the keys
# you have. The gateway loads this file at startup and any provider whose key is
# empty is DISABLED automatically — so you can start with just one key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env

# Where to get each key:
#   E_INFRA_API_KEY     e-Infra CZ LLM portal (https://llm.ai.e-infra.cz) — endpoint returns 401 without it
#   OPENCODE_API_KEY    https://opencode.ai/console -> API -> Personal API keys
#                       (required even for the free models; calls from outside the OpenCode client get 403)
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY  https://openrouter.ai/keys (covers free AND paid models; credits checked via /auth/key)
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY    https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys (paid; balance checked via /user/balance)
#   AA_API_KEY          https://artificialanalysis.ai (free signup; ~100 req/day; used by refresh.py for benchmark ranks)

E_INFRA_API_KEY=
OPENCODE_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
AA_API_KEY=

# Optional. Command used to resolve OpenCode session IDs to human titles for the
# dashboard. Defaults to `opencode api get /api/session`; set to an empty value
# to disable title resolution entirely (e.g. in tests or headless deploys).
# ROUTER_TITLES_CMD=opencode api get /api/session
